<p>The openssl API package can be obtained from the include folder of the openssl tool used in Step 1 to generate the RSA keys.</p>

<p>Let me explain how to integrate openssl into an iOS project:</p>

<h3 id="1-download-the-openssl-library">1. Download the openssl library</h3>
<p><a href="https://github.com/st3fan/ios-openssl">openssl for iOS download</a></p>

<h3 id="2-import-into-the-project">2. Import into the project</h3>

<p>Drag the openssl library <em>(the folder containing <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">include</code> &amp; <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lib</code>)</em> into the project</p>

<p>Then go to project targets -&gt; <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Build Settings</code></p>

<ul>
  <li>Find <strong>Header Search Paths</strong>, add <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"${SRCROOT}/Libraries/openssl/include"</code> for your project</li>
  <li>Find <strong>Library Search Paths</strong>, add <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">"${SRCROOT}/Libraries/openssl/lib"</code></li>
</ul>

<p>Then it should work. If you run into problems in the middle, check whether the directory is correct — theoretically it should be fine.</p>

